<title>SOUTH AFRICA: WALTONS EARNINGS SLUMP, YEAR CHANGED.</title>
<headline>WALTONS EARNINGS SLUMP, YEAR CHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months ended Feb 28, 1997 </p>
<p>		 (millions of rand unless indicated)</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)  50.0   vs  69.4</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)   27.8   vs  66.8</p>
<p>    Attrib income	 27.09  vs  57.01</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		 51.22  vs  98.41</p>
<p>    Tax		     21.37  vs  35.98</p>
<p>    Interest paid	 44.45  vs  44.06</p>
<p>    Turnover	    1,559.48 vs 1,262.04</p>
<p>Full name: Waltons Stationery Company Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said the causes of its poor perfomance had</p>
<p>been identified and a planned strategy was in place to</p>
<p>restructure management, rationalise operations, improve</p>
<p>financial reporting and update information systems.</p>
<p>It has changed its year-end to June 30 in line with that of</p>
<p>majority shareholder Pepkor . Its policy is to declare</p>
<p>only one dividend a year.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
